 19.1 m, area 988 m2. No official dimension was found to check it against, so confidence stays approximate.", "name": "PSI Injector 2 hall (WIHA)", "osm": {"elements": ["way/28028422"], "timestamp": "2026-10-25T11:05:26Z"}, "provenance": {"confidence": "approximate", "locator": "OSM way/28028422 version 2 (2011-09-30T09:39:04Z) fetched 2026-10-25T11:05:26Z; Arealplan 18.11.2015 legend line 'WIHA Injektorhalle 2 B6'", "note": "OpenStreetMap alone yields at most 'approximate'.", "quote": null, "sources": ["src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015", "src:psi-geo-osm-wiha-hall"], "verified_at": "2026-10-25"}, "representation": "georeferenced", "site_id": "site:psi-villigen", "state_segments": null, "status": null}, {"accuracy_m": 8, "checks": [], "depth_m": null, "entity_id": null, "entity_name": null, "entity_type": null, "feature_type": "building", "geometry": {"coordinates": [[[8.223011, 47.5365368], [8.2234732, 47.5364836], [8.223351, 47.5360262], [8.2233168, 47.5360303], [8.2232834, 47.5359053], [8.2231642, 47.5359195], [8.2230264, 47.5354027], [8.222722, 47.5354365], [8.2228094, 47.5357919], [8.2228908, 47.5360773], [8.223011, 47.5365368]]], "type": "Polygon"}, "id": "geometry:psi-sinq-building", "level_id": "surface", "license": {"attribution": "© OpenStreetMap contributors", "name": "ODbL-1.0", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}, "measured": {"area_m2": 3643.347623593603, "centroid": [8.2230792, 47.5360185], "length_m": 318.508057638322}, "method": "OpenStreetMap way 694278565 (building, name 'SINQ') used verbatim. PSI's site-map legend lists the SINQ halls as 'WNHA Neutronenhalle' and 'WNLA Neutronenleiterhalle' (src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015); the OSM outline (124.8 m x 35.4 m, area 3643 m2, L-shaped) carries the name SINQ and was not matched to either code individually. No official dimension was found to check it against.", "name": "PSI SINQ spallation neutron source building", "osm": {"elements": ["way/694278565"], "timestamp": "2026-10-25T11:05:29Z"}, "provenance": {"confidence": "approximate", "locator": "OSM way/694278565 version 3 (2024-04-21T15:26:44Z) fetched 2026-10-25T11:05:29Z; Arealplan 18.11.2015 legend lines 'WNHA Neutronenhalle B7' and 'WNLA Neutronenleiterhalle B7'", "note": "OpenStreetMap alone yields at most 'approximate'.", "quote": null, "sources": ["src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015", "src:psi-geo-osm-sinq-building"], "verified_at": "2026-10-25"}, "representation": "georeferenced", "site_id": "site:psi-villigen", "state_segments": null, "status": null}, {"accuracy_m": 8, "checks": [], "depth_m": null, "entity_id": null, "entity_name": null, "entity_type": null, "feature_type": "building", "geometry": {"coordinates": [[[8.2219086, 47.5366733], [8.2222404, 47.5366355], [8.2222891, 47.5366287], [8.2222625, 47.5365161], [8.2218818, 47.5365653], [8.2219086, 47.5366733]]], "type": "Polygon"}, "id": "geometry:psi-ucn-hall-wnab", "level_id": "surface", "license": {"attribution": "© OpenStreetMap contributors", "name": "ODbL-1.0", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright"}, "measured": {"area_m2": 362.6121905230658, "centroid": [8.2220871, 47.5365959], "length_m": 82.94689473587702}, "method": "OpenStreetMap way 736230166 (building, name 'WNAB') used verbatim; PSI's site-map legend gives 'WNAB UCN-Halle' and 'WMFA UCN-Betriebsgebäude' (src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015). Footprint 29.2 m x 12.8 m, area 363 m2. The UCN operations building WMFA has no named OSM outline and is not drawn.", "name": "PSI ultracold-neutron hall (WNAB)", "osm": {"elements": ["way/736230166"], "timestamp": "2026-10-25T11:05:31Z"}, "provenance": {"confidence": "approximate", "locator": "OSM way/736230166 version 2 (2024-04-21T15:26:44Z) fetched 2026-10-25T11:05:31Z; Arealplan 18.11.2015 legend line 'WNAB UCN-Halle A7'", "note": "OpenStreetMap alone yields at most 'approximate'.", "quote": null, "sources": ["src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015", "src:psi-geo-osm-wnab-ucn-hall"], "verified_at": "2026-10-25"}, "representation": "georeferenced", "site_id": "site:psi-villigen", "state_segments": null, "status": null}], "map": {"aliases": [], "center": {"approximate": true, "kind": "campus", "lat": 47.5375192, "lon": 8.2250675, "precision_m": 300}, "coverage": {"researched": "partial", "tier": "C"}, "extent_m": 800, "facility_id": "facility:psi", "id": "map:psi", "levels": [{"depth_m": null, "id": "surface", "kind": "surface", "name": "Surface"}], "linked_map_ids": [], "links": {"website": null}, "name": "PSI — Villigen and Wurenlingen campus", "schematics": [], "site_ids": ["site:psi-villigen"], "summary": {"plain": "The Paul Scherrer Institute's two-bank campus beside the River Aare in Aargau, Switzerland, drawn to scale from OpenStreetMap: the campus boundary, the 134 m by 52 m experimental hall of the proton accelerator, the Injector 2 hall, the SINQ neutron source and the ultracold-neutron hall, and the other buildings. The Ring Cyclotron itself could not be placed because PSI's own site map does not say which building holds it."}, "type": "map", "unlocated": [{"backlog": "Find a PSI document that names the building of the Ring Cyclotron (its building code in the Arealplan legend, or a layout drawing with a scale bar and coordinates), or an official GIS layer; then take that building from OSM by its four-letter code (the OSM names carry the codes). The 2015 Arealplan is a graphic with a text legend; it was read for the legend only and not traced. Candidate leads, unconfirmed: the building codes WHFA (RF building) and the WEHA/WIHA halls are adjacent to the machine area, and the sourced 'ø15m' size (Seidel 2009) is a 15 m machine inside a vault, so the building is larger than the machine; a PSI beam-line layout drawing with building codes, or the 'HIPA info' elog layout, would settle it.", "entity_id": "accelerator:psi-hipa", "entity_name": "High Intensity Proton Accelerator", "entity_type": "accelerator", "reason": "The Ring Cyclotron (a 590 MeV machine 'ø15m' across, src:psi-geo-seidel-2009) is not placed: PSI's own site-map legend (src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015) names an experimental hall (WEHA), an Injector 2 hall (WIHA), a neutron hall, a UCN hall and a 'Nukleonenhalle' (WNAA) but has no entry that says which building holds the Ring Cyclotron, and PSI's HIPA page and talks show its layout only as an unscaled diagram. No building was guessed from its shape. What the map does show of the HIPA complex is context only: the experimental hall WEHA (drawn as a hall, size-checked), the Injector 2 hall WIHA, the SINQ building and the UCN hall WNAB. The Cockcroft-Walton injector and the beam transfer tunnels are not located either. Checked again on 2026-10-25: PSI's own Ring Cyclotron page gives the machine's radii (injection 2.1 m, extraction 4.5 m) and no location; the HIPA, Injector 2 and Kiselev (2024) pages and talks, the HB2012 and Cyclotrons 2022 papers and the full Arealplan legend (which lists WEHA, WIHA, WHFA 'Hochfrequenzgebaeude' and 'Niederenergieareal C' WYCA but no 'Ringzyklotron' entry) were searched again; none says which building holds the Ring Cyclotron. The Injector 2 hall WIHA is named 'Injektorhalle 2' by PSI's legend, so it is drawn as context but deliberately not attached to accelerator:psi-hipa, whose main machine is the Ring Cyclotron.", "sources": ["src:facilities-verify-psi-hipa-page", "src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015", "src:psi-geo-kiselev-impact-2024", "src:psi-geo-ring-cyclotron-page", "src:psi-geo-seidel-2009"]}]}, "schema": "hep-atlas/0.2", "source_titles": {"src:facilities-verify-psi-hipa-page": {"source_type": "official_facility_site", "title": "High Intensity Proton Accelerator Facility | PSI Center for Accelerator Science and Engineering -- official PSI page", "url": "https://www.psi.ch/en/cas/hipa"}, "src:geo-psi-osm-campus-boundary": {"source_type": "openstreetmap", "title": "OpenStreetMap ways 28028409 / 26680824 / 26680821: Paul Scherrer Institut campus (Villigen and Wurenlingen sides)", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/28028409"}, "src:psi-geo-arealplan-2015": {"source_type": "official_facility_site", "title": "PSI Arealplan 18.11.2015 (site map with building-code legend, PSI-West and PSI-Ost)", "url": "https://indico.psi.ch/event/4127/attachments/7754/9862/PSIsitemapESS.pdf"}, "src:psi-geo-kiselev-impact-2024": {"source_type": "project_document", "title": "Projekt IMPACT an HIPA (D. Kiselev, Festsymposium 50 Jahre HIPA, 27.2.2024)", "url": "https://indico.psi.ch/event/14948/contributions/46875/attachments/27289/51331/05_Kiselev%20IMPACT-HIPA50s.pdf"}, "src:psi-geo-osm-campus-buildings": {"source_type": "openstreetmap", "title": "OpenStreetMap extract: building footprints on the PSI West and PSI East campus", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/#map=17/47.5375/8.2251"}, "src:psi-geo-osm-sinq-building": {"source_type": "openstreetmap", "title": "OpenStreetMap way 694278565: building 'SINQ' (spallation neutron source)", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/694278565"}, "src:psi-geo-osm-weha-hall": {"source_type": "openstreetmap", "title": "OpenStreetMap way 28028423: building 'SμS/Particle Physics - WEHA' (PSI experimental hall)", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/28028423"}, "src:psi-geo-osm-wiha-hall": {"source_type": "openstreetmap", "title": "OpenStreetMap way 28028422: building 'WIHA' (Injektorhalle 2)", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/28028422"}, "src:psi-geo-osm-wnab-ucn-hall": {"source_type": "openstreetmap", "title": "OpenStreetMap way 736230166: building 'WNAB' (UCN-Halle)", "url": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/736230166"}, "src:psi-geo-ring-cyclotron-page": {"source_type": "official_facility_site", "title": "The Ring Cyclotron (PSI, Center for Accelerator Science and Engineering)", "url": "https://www.psi.ch/en/cas/ring"}, "src:psi-geo-seidel-2009": {"source_type": "project_document", "title": "Performance of the PSI High Power Proton Accelerator (M. Seidel, A. C. Mezger; talk at J-PARC, 7 July 2009)", "url": "https://www2.kek.jp/accl/legacy/seminar/file/mike_seidel_PSI_accelerators.pdf"}}, "version": "0b0d250cf3575fc6"}
